+  <p><strong>Review only:</strong> <code class="long"><span class="nw">/sc:auggie-review</span> <span class="nw">--no-post-pr</span> <span class="nw">--no-remediation-offer</span></code> on a PR, a diff or a snapshot keeps the findings local. Do not add commits, pushes or a PR to findings-only work.</p>
+  <p><strong>Ship only when it is requested and authorized</strong>, in this order:</p>
   <ul>
-    <li><strong>Commit locally</strong> on your feature branch. Do not push yet.</li>
-    <li><strong>Bug review:</strong> <code>/code-review</code>. <strong>Security review</strong> if you touched login, permissions, secrets, user input or file paths: <code>/security-review</code>. Commit the fixes.</li>
-    <li><strong>Branch review:</strong> <code>/sc:auggie-review</code> on the whole branch, kept local with <code>--no-post-pr</code>.</li>
-    <li><strong>Push only after your lead approves.</strong></li>
-    <li><strong>Open the PR</strong> with <code>/sc:pr-submit --monitor 3</code>. It fixes confirmed review findings of Medium severity or higher (lower ones are only reported) and failing CI checks (the automatic tests and checks GitHub runs on the PR).</li>
+    <li><strong>Commit locally</strong> on your feature branch, only when authorized.</li>
+    <li><strong>Bug review:</strong> <code>/code-review</code>. <strong>Security review</strong> if you touched login, permissions, secrets, user input or file paths: <code>/security-review</code>. Authorize and record any fixes before the branch review.</li>
+    <li><strong>Branch review:</strong> <code class="long"><span class="nw">/sc:auggie-review</span> <span class="nw">--diff origin/&lt;main branch&gt;...HEAD</span> <span class="nw">--no-post-pr</span> <span class="nw">--no-remediation-offer</span></code>.</li>
+    <li><strong>Push only with your lead's approval.</strong></li>
+    <li><strong>Open the PR</strong> with <code>/sc:pr-submit</code> and the one monitor ceiling you chose (below).</li>
   </ul>
